\vspace{-8pt}
\[ \text{Moles of NaOH} = \frac{5\ \text{g}}{40\ \text{g mol}^{-1}} = 0.125\ \text{mol} \]
Volume of the solution in litres = 450 mL / 1000 mL L$^{-1}$\\
Using equation (2.8),
\[ \begin{aligned}
\text{Molarity} &= \frac{0.125\ \text{mol} \times 1000\ \text{mL L}^{-1}}{450\ \text{mL}} = 0.278\ \text{M}\\[4pt]
&= 0.278\ \text{mol L}^{-1}\\
&= 0.278\ \text{mol dm}^{-3}
\end{aligned} \]
\end{minipage}
