If N$_2$ gas is bubbled through water at 293 K, how many millimoles of N$_2$ gas would dissolve in 1 litre of water? Assume that N$_2$ exerts a partial pressure of 0.987 bar. Given that Henry's law constant for N$_2$ at 293 K is 76.48 \textit{k}bar.
