\[ \text{m} \;=\; \frac{w_2/\text{M}_2}{w_1/1000} \;=\; \frac{1000 \times w_2}{M_2 \times w_1} \tag{1.31} \]
\hspace*{1.5em}Substituting the value of molality in equation (1.30) we get
\[ \Delta T_\text{b} \;=\; \frac{K_\text{b} \times 1000 \times w_2}{M_2 \times w_1} \tag{1.32} \]
\[ M_2 \;=\; \frac{1000 \times w_2 \times K_\text{b}}{\Delta T_\text{b} \times w_1} \tag{1.33} \]
\hspace*{1.5em}Thus, in order to determine $M_2$, molar mass of the solute, known mass of solute in a known mass of the solvent is taken and $\Delta T_\text{b}$ is determined experimentally for a known solvent whose $K_\text{b}$ value is known.
\end{minipage}

